{
  "tool_analysis": "# Tool Analysis for Shipment Management\n\n## Step Analysis\nThe recorded steps demonstrate a comprehensive shipment search and filtering workflow in Magento admin:\n1. Navigated to Magento admin and logged in (credentials already handled)\n2. Accessed Sales > Shipments page\n3. Discovered and interacted with all filter controls\n4. Demonstrated key search/filter operations:\n   - Search by shipment number (using \"Shipment\" field)\n   - Search by order number (using \"Order #\" field)\n   - Filter by date range (using \"Order Date\" from/to fields)\n   - Apply filters using \"Apply Filters\" button\n5. Discovered additional controls: column selector, export options, advanced filters, dropdown filters\n\n## Task Definition\nCreate a tool to search and filter shipments in Magento admin using various criteria including shipment number, order number, date ranges, order status, and other available filters.\n\n## Action Plan\n1. Navigate to shipments page (already authenticated)\n2. Open filters panel\n3. Fill in search/filter criteria based on input parameters\n4. Apply filters\n5. Extract filtered results\n\n## Variable Identification\nBased on the demonstrated interactions, these input parameters are needed:\n1. `shipment_number` - Search by shipment number (uses \"Shipment\" field)\n2. `order_number` - Search by order number (uses \"Order #\" field)\n3. `order_date_from` - Filter by order date range start\n4. `order_date_to` - Filter by order date range end\n5. `order_status` - Filter by order status (dropdown)\n6. `purchased_from` - Filter by store view (dropdown)\n7. `customer_group` - Filter by customer group (dropdown)\n8. `payment_method` - Filter by payment method (dropdown)\n9. `ship_to_name` - Filter by ship-to name\n10. `customer_name` - Filter by customer name\n11. `email` - Filter by email\n12. `total_qty_from` - Filter by total quantity range start\n13. `total_qty_to` - Filter by total quantity range end\n\n## Step Optimization\n- Navigation to shipments page is essential (starting point)\n- Opening filters panel is required to access all filter controls\n- All filter fields should be filled based on provided parameters\n- Apply filters button is required to execute search\n- Extract results to show filtered shipment data\n- Use deterministic steps with elementHash where available\n- Add wait steps for UI responsiveness\n- Note: The agent is already logged in, so no authentication steps needed",
